  sha256 6ffaa56681406aa55073cb9c5ae296edd6659730ff8d73793c5655a77483e78c  tavern_upstream.py (upstream 2.3.1, as received)

How to check it (any one is enough; they read the same bytes):
  sha256sum polygram/mcp/tavern_upstream.py                     (GNU/Linux, msys2)
  shasum -a 256 polygram/mcp/tavern_upstream.py                 (macOS)
  certutil -hashfile polygram\mcp\tavern_upstream.py SHA256     (Windows)
and compare with the line above.  tests/tavernface-tests.sh does it too, and goes red when a byte
is planted (its prove-red).

Where updates come from: the tavern.py drop Bryant posts in the Tavern room, or the tavern.py
inside his Tavern-Setup.bat (`python tavern.py build-setup` prints both hashes).  To take a new
version: copy it in whole as tavern_upstream.py, change the sha256 line above and the pin in
tests/tavernface-tests.sh, and run the tests.  Never edit the file itself; changes for Bryant go
to him as a patch (projects/garden-pony/ keeps the working copy and the patches).

